      "writtenOn": "2020-04-14T05:17:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of these follow the common pattern of:\nDefine variablefunc \"foo\" based on env variable \"bar\" that returns value of \"bar\" if its set, or return a \"default\" value. I think its better to make a config of these three and run a for-loop to define them, so that its easier to add new ones. Something like:\n\n```\ntype rbeVariableDefinition {\n    envVar string\n    default string\n}\n\nvar (\n    rbeVars :\u003d map[string]rbeVariableDefinition{\n        \"REWrapper\": rbeVariableDefinition{envVar: \"RBE_WRAPPER\", default: \"prebuilts/remoteexecution-client/live/rewrapper\"},\n        ...\n    }\n)\n\nfunc init() {\n    ...\n\n    for var, def :\u003d range rbeVars {\n        pctx.VariableFunc(var, func(ctx android.PackageVarContext) string {\n\t\tif override :\u003d ctx.Config().Getenv(def.envVar); override !\u003d \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn override\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn def.default\n\t})\n    }\n}\n```\n\nwdyt?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 260,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 3
      },
